All relevant documentation on compiling and running DEGAS 2 is now
contained in the manual. See the section there entitled "Compiling DEGAS 2".
The manual can be found at:

1. In text form as a TeX file in Doc/degas2_all.tex,
2. This directory also contains HTML, DVI, PostScript, and PDF versions
   of this same file.
3. These are all accessible via the Web from the URL:

   http://w3.pppl.gov/degas2

Derivation of Data Files

The two data files in this dirctory were created for use with this example.
h2desorbc.nc is the same as that in the data directory except that the
velocity distribution (in pf_eval_name) used for the "desorbed" H2 is 
maxwell_flux instead of cosine. The value of pf_data_tab associated with
the variable energy_out was correspondingly changed from 150000 (fourth
element in the pf_data_tab array) to 50000. With this change, 
energy_out goes from 1.5 t_wall to 0.5 t_wall; this is required for
use with the maxwell_flux velocity distribution.

The second file d2d2_bgktest.nc was created manually as a much simpler
version of the dd_neut.nc file in the data directory. The reaction
rate is just a constant, 1.1e-10 cm^3/s. This controls the rate of all of
the collisions in the problem and should yield (for the chosen boundary
condition on the velocity) Knudsen numbers of roughly 1.

